"""An orthographic r + labial-consonant detector.

The strongest response is to pieces ending in rv (especially ERV).  There
are weaker rb/rw responses.  Splitting r and v/b/w between two pieces also
counts, including Cyrillic р-в/б.  A little response persists into the next
piece of the same word.  These are approximate spelling rules, not meanings.
"""
READS = ()

# For a join: base, single-letter bonus, long-piece adjustment, preceding e.
JOINS = {
    'rv': (2.3, 3.1, -2.7, 1.0),
    'rb': (1.0, 1.1, -1.2, 0.4),
    'rw': (1.0, 0.4, -1.4, 0.7),
    'рв': (2.9, 1.6, 0.5, 0.0),
    'рб': (1.4, 1.5, 0.0, 1.4),
